{
  "$comment": "THE declaration of omx-eq8: the CLAP and LV2 faces and the parameter header are generated from this file by tools/gen.mjs. Parameter order is append-only. The travels are the console's own EQ_FREQ_RANGE, EQ_GAIN_RANGE, EQ_Q_RANGE (a notch's Q reaches EQ_NOTCH_Q_RANGE), HPF_FREQ_RANGE and LPF_FREQ_RANGE, read as omx-dsp's omx_contract_limits.h carries them. The band count is a compile-time 8; band types are 0 bell, 1 low shelf, 2 high shelf, 3 notch, 4 allpass1, 5 allpass2, labelled as the console's bundle labels them; a slope takes 12 or 24 dB/oct and nothing between. No MOD GUI: tools/modgui-gen.mjs does not draw selectors.",
  "stem": "omx-eq8",
  "kernel": "eq8",
  "name": "omx eq8",
  "noun": "8-band EQ",
  "vendor": "openmixer",
  "url": "https://github.com/FreeMixer/omx-plugins",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "description": "The OpenMixer console's channel EQ, 8-band form: eight parametric bands (bell, shelves, notch, allpass) and a high-pass and a low-pass filter at 12 or 24 dB/oct, stereo, zero latency. The DSP is omx-dsp's <omxdsp/fx/omx_eq_instance.h>, the console's own EQ; every band ships off, so a racked instance is a wire.",
  "clap": {
    "id": "org.openmixer.eq8",
    "features": [
      "audio-effect",
      "equalizer",
      "stereo"
    ]
  },
  "lv2": {
